==============================================================================
E2. optional strengthening (auditor): tilted cycle lemma at gamma = 1 on the minus sheet
==============================================================================
steps x_j + alpha/t, o = ceil(t/alpha) + 2 (so S_t <= -2 alpha and the tilted total is <= -alpha < 0); rotate after
the maximal tilted partial sum; then S'_i <= -i alpha/t for 1 <= i <= t, so 2^(-S'_i) >= 3^(i/t) >= 1 + (i/t) ln 3 and
T_-^i(n) >= n + n (i/t) ln 3 - (3/2)^i > n for n >= 2^t (margin inequality 2^t (i/t) ln 3 >= (3/2)^i, all 1<=i<=t):
this would give c X^(h*)/log^(3/2) X on the minus sheet too, with the same C(t,o)/t count.
